  "note": "parse_port_directions(behavioural_v) subset for the 69 cells puzzle.gds uses, recorded 2026-11-15 with the pre-issue-106 filter (_POWER_PINS = {VPWR, VGND, VPB, VNB}) so the swap to verilog_netlist.POWER_PINS can be checked against it: tools/sim/selftest_celltable.py asserts this map is unchanged for these 69 cells. Cells outside this set are deliberately NOT pinned: the swap drops KAPWR from the lpflow_*kapwr_* cells (issue #106, intended behaviour change). The two cells in cells_absent_after_filter (fill/tap: VPWR/VGND/VPB/VNB only) have no signal pins, so the filtered map is empty and parse_port_directions omits them -- under both filters. Recorded from the volare install named in source, and the self-test re-parses that same path rather than resolve_sky130_models(): a golden baseline is only meaningful against the install it was recorded from, and the host may resolve a different one. (The newer ~/.ciel open_pdks install declares ports as `input wire X;`; since issue #98 widened _DIR_RE that style parses too -- measured 418/437 cells there -- so the pin is about provenance, not a parse limitation.)",
